menu "WiSense CSI Receiver Configuration"

    config RX_CSI_UART_BAUDRATE
        int "UART baud rate (bps)"
        default 921600
        range 115200 2000000
        help
            Baud rate for serial communication with host/Python reader.
            Default is 921600 baud (~92.16 kB/s), which provides >50% headroom
            for 100 binary frames/sec (~41.6 kB/s). Configurable via menuconfig
            in compliance with the project-wide constraint against hardcoded
            operational parameters.

    config RX_CSI_WIFI_CHANNEL
        int "WiFi Channel (1-13)"
        default 11
        range 1 13
        help
            2.4 GHz primary WiFi channel to tune the receiver front-end,
            matching CONFIG_TX_BEACON_WIFI_CHANNEL. Channel 11 is selected by
            default for low ambient co-channel interference in our laboratory baseline.

    config RX_CSI_FILTER_MAC
        string "Transmitter MAC Filter (hex format XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX)"
        default "1a:00:00:00:00:00"
        help
            Expected source MAC address of the transmitter beacon (tx_beacon).
            Frames from any other source MAC are discarded immediately inside
            the WiFi CSI callback (<2 microseconds), isolating ambient traffic.

    config RX_CSI_QUEUE_DEPTH
        int "FreeRTOS CSI queue depth (frames)"
        default 32
        range 8 128
        help
            Maximum number of CSI frames buffered between the high-priority
            WiFi RX callback and the UART transmission task. At 100 pps, a depth
            of 32 provides 320 ms of buffering against UART transmission bursts.

    config RX_CSI_LOG_INTERVAL_SEC
        int "Serial status log interval (seconds)"
        default 1
        range 1 60
        help
            Frequency in seconds at which reception health statistics
            ([RX_STAT] count, window packets, uptime, achieved pps, dropped,
            ambient filtered, and free heap) are output to the serial monitor.

    config RX_CSI_OUTPUT_BINARY
        bool "Enable binary framed CSI streaming"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, transmits structured binary frames with 4-byte magic sync
            marker, fixed metadata header, raw CSI payload, and CRC-16 checksum
            over UART. If disabled, receiver operates in silent/diagnostic mode,
            logging only periodic [RX_STAT] telemetry.

endmenu
